{# The front-end home page.

   Craft installs with no content and no templates: `templates/` is a directory
   craftcms/craft ships with one placeholder in it, and a site whose
   templates/index.twig does not exist answers 404 on `/`. That is a correct
   404 -- there is genuinely nothing to show yet -- but it is also the first
   thing anyone sees, and a health probe reading it cannot tell "installed,
   empty" from "broken".

   So this is a placeholder, and it says so. Delete it, or replace it with the
   real home page, as soon as there is one. #}
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="{{ craft.app.language }}">
<head>
    <meta charset="utf-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
    <meta name="robots" content="noindex">
    <title>{{ siteName }}</title>
    <style>
        :root { color-scheme: light dark; }
        body { margin: 0; min-height: 100vh; display: grid; place-items: center;
               font: 16px/1.6 -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, "Segoe UI", Roboto, sans-serif; }
        main { max-width: 34rem; padding: 2rem; }
        h1 { font-size: 1.6rem; margin: 0 0 .5rem; }
        p { margin: 0 0 1rem; opacity: .8; }
        code { font-family: ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, Menlo, monospace; }
    </style>
</head>
<body>
<main>
    <h1>{{ siteName }}</h1>
    <p>Craft {{ craft.app.version }} is installed and this is the placeholder
        home page, <code>templates/index.twig</code>. Replace it with your own.</p>
    <p><a href="{{ cpUrl() }}">Control panel</a></p>
</main>
</body>
</html>
